d2d1: record the WIC seed state at the OUTCOME, not at the intent

Premiere's splash screen rendered its left half as a WHITE BOX for 1-2 seconds
before correcting itself. User-confirmed cause and fix.

d2d_wic_render_target_reset_state() recorded "this texture holds this bitmap's
pixels" -- pool_last_bitmap / pool_last_gen / pool_last_gen_valid -- BEFORE
attempting the seed:

    rt->pool_last_gen = gen;
    rt->pool_last_gen_valid = TRUE;
    ...
    if (seed_from_bitmap(rt)) { }
    else if (rt->pool_rtv)    { ClearRenderTargetView(...); }   <-- texture CLEARED

When the seed fails the texture is cleared instead, and the record still claims
a match. The next time that pooled target is handed the same bitmap with an
unchanged write generation, the skip fires and it publishes the CLEARED
texture. It only corrected itself when the app happened to redraw the region --
hence "white for a second or two, then fine".

Now the record happens once the outcome is known: set on a successful seed,
explicitly forgotten on the clear path, and forgotten on the third path too
(seed failed with no RTV to clear) where we genuinely do not know what the
texture holds.

⭐ SAME MISTAKE AS THE MASK VERDICT EARLIER TODAY, in a different file. device.c
logged "bounding box in force" at the DECLINE, before the stencil had a chance
to carry the mask. Here the seed bookkeeping recorded success at the INTENT.
Both are state written before the thing it describes has happened.
RULE: record/report at the OUTCOME, never at the intent.

⚠️ Shipped in 11.10-61, so it is not a 62 regression -- a pooled WIC target
publishing a cleared texture is exactly the class of defect that produces
intermittent blank UI regions, and may account for sightings attributed
elsewhere. 11.10-62's tarball predates this fix and must be repackaged.

Confirmed with NEUTRON_WIC_SEED_SKIP=0 first (splash correct => the skip was
the cause), then with the fix and the optimisation left ON (splash correct).

--- a/dlls/d2d1/wic_render_target.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/wic_render_target.c
@@ -851,9 +851,11 @@
      *
      * ⚠️ Fails SAFE on every uncertainty: a bitmap we have not seen before, a windowscodecs
      * without v3 (DLLs are staged individually), or any error -- all fall through and seed. */
+    ULONG gen = 0;
+    BOOL have_gen = FALSE;
+
     {
         INeutronWicGpuBitmap3 *gen_iface;
-        ULONG gen = 0;
         BOOL untouched = FALSE;
         static int enabled = -1;
 
@@ -876,14 +878,16 @@
                 untouched = rt->bitmap == rt->pool_last_bitmap
                         && rt->pool_last_gen_valid && gen == rt->pool_last_gen;
             gen_iface->lpVtbl->Release(gen_iface);
-            rt->pool_last_gen = gen;
-            rt->pool_last_gen_valid = TRUE;
-        }
-        else
-        {
-            rt->pool_last_gen_valid = FALSE;
+            have_gen = TRUE;
         }
-        rt->pool_last_bitmap = rt->bitmap;
+        /* ⛔ Do NOT record "the texture holds this bitmap's pixels" here. That is not known yet --
+         * the seed below can FAIL, and the failure path CLEARS the texture instead. Recording it
+         * up front is what put a white box on Premiere's splash for 1-2 s (2026-08-25): seed
+         * fails -> texture cleared -> bookkeeping still says "matches" -> the next reuse of this
+         * target with the same bitmap and an unchanged generation SKIPS the seed and publishes the
+         * cleared texture. It only corrected itself when the app happened to redraw.
+         * The record now happens after the outcome is known -- same rule as the mask verdict in
+         * device.c: report/record at the OUTCOME, never at the intent. */
 
         if (neutron_perf())
         {
@@ -902,13 +906,27 @@
 
     if (d2d_wic_render_target_seed_from_bitmap(rt))
     {
-        /* texture now matches the bitmap; nothing further to do */
+        /* The texture now genuinely holds this bitmap's pixels -- NOW it is true, so now record
+         * it. A later reuse may legitimately skip the seed on the strength of this. */
+        rt->pool_last_bitmap = rt->bitmap;
+        rt->pool_last_gen = gen;
+        rt->pool_last_gen_valid = have_gen;
     }
     else if (rt->pool_rtv)
     {
         ID3D10Texture2D_GetDevice(rt->readback_texture, &device);
         ID3D10Device_ClearRenderTargetView(device, rt->pool_rtv, clear_colour);
         ID3D10Device_Release(device);
+        /* The texture holds the CLEAR COLOUR, not this bitmap. Anything remembered about a
+         * previous tenant is now false -- forget it, or the next reuse skips a seed it needs. */
+        rt->pool_last_bitmap = NULL;
+        rt->pool_last_gen_valid = FALSE;
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        /* Seed failed and there was nothing to clear: we have no idea what the texture holds. */
+        rt->pool_last_bitmap = NULL;
+        rt->pool_last_gen_valid = FALSE;
     }
 }
 
